{"code":"25-4013.00","title":"Museum Technicians and Conservators","description":"Restore, maintain, or prepare objects in museum collections for storage, research, or exhibit. May work with specimens such as fossils, skeletal parts, or botanicals; or artifacts, textiles, or art. May identify and record objects or install and arrange them in exhibits. Includes book or document conservators.","jobZone":5,"kinds":{"R":{"score":5.67,"share":0.3166},"I":{"score":3.21,"share":0.1498},"A":{"score":3.14,"share":0.1451},"S":{"score":2.64,"share":0.1112},"E":{"score":1.51,"share":0.0346},"C":{"score":4.58,"share":0.2427}},"highPoints":["R","C"],"tasks":[{"id":3808,"text":"Determine whether objects need repair and choose the safest and most effective method of repair.","core":true,"importance":4.83,"relevance":100,"frequency":4.71},{"id":3813,"text":"Specialize in particular materials or types of object, such as documents and books, paintings, decorative arts, textiles, metals, or architectural materials.","core":true,"importance":4.74,"relevance":95.83,"frequency":5.59},{"id":3814,"text":"Recommend preservation procedures, such as control of temperature and humidity, to curatorial and building staff.","core":true,"importance":4.67,"relevance":100,"frequency":3.38},{"id":3806,"text":"Install, arrange, assemble, and prepare artifacts for exhibition, ensuring the artifacts' safety, reporting their status and condition, and identifying and correcting any problems with the set up.","core":true,"importance":4.59,"relevance":95.83,"frequency":3.74},{"id":3820,"text":"Study object documentation or conduct standard chemical and physical tests to ascertain the object's age, composition, original appearance, need for treatment or restoration, and appropriate preservation method.","core":true,"importance":4.52,"relevance":100,"frequency":4.13},{"id":3809,"text":"Clean objects, such as paper, textiles, wood, metal, glass, rock, pottery, and furniture, using cleansers, solvents, soap solutions, and polishes.","core":true,"importance":4.5,"relevance":100,"frequency":4.5},{"id":3818,"text":"Repair, restore, and reassemble artifacts, designing and fabricating missing or broken parts, to restore them to their original appearance and prevent deterioration.","core":true,"importance":4.46,"relevance":100,"frequency":4.75},{"id":3822,"text":"Perform tests and examinations to establish storage and conservation requirements, policies, and procedures.","core":true,"importance":4.46,"relevance":100,"frequency":3.71},{"id":3819,"text":"Prepare reports on the operation of conservation laboratories, documenting the condition of artifacts, treatment options, and the methods of preservation and repair used.","core":true,"importance":4.39,"relevance":95.83,"frequency":3.61},{"id":18643,"text":"Direct and supervise curatorial, technical, and student staff in the handling, mounting, care, and storage of art objects.","core":true,"importance":4.38,"relevance":100,"frequency":4},{"id":18644,"text":"Photograph objects for documentation.","core":true,"importance":4.29,"relevance":100,"frequency":3.75},{"id":21065,"text":"Enter information about museum collections into computer databases.","core":true,"importance":4.14,"relevance":91.67,"frequency":4.32},{"id":3823,"text":"Plan and conduct research to develop and improve methods of restoring and preserving specimens.","core":true,"importance":4.04,"relevance":95.83,"frequency":3.26},{"id":3810,"text":"Prepare artifacts for storage and shipping.","core":true,"importance":3.96,"relevance":100,"frequency":3.25},{"id":3826,"text":"Preserve or direct preservation of objects, using plaster, resin, sealants, hardeners, and shellac.","core":false,"importance":3.58,"relevance":52.17,"frequency":2.83},{"id":3817,"text":"Perform on-site field work which may involve interviewing people, inspecting and identifying artifacts, note-taking, viewing sites and collections, and repainting exhibition spaces.","core":true,"importance":3.52,"relevance":87.5,"frequency":2.67},{"id":3824,"text":"Notify superior when restoration of artifacts requires outside experts.","core":true,"importance":3.45,"relevance":91.67,"frequency":1.91},{"id":3825,"text":"Estimate cost of restoration work.","core":true,"importance":3.3,"relevance":87.5,"frequency":3.33},{"id":3815,"text":"Classify and assign registration numbers to artifacts and supervise inventory control.","core":false,"importance":3.22,"relevance":37.5,"frequency":2.89},{"id":3807,"text":"Coordinate exhibit installations, assisting with design, constructing displays, dioramas, display cases, and models, and ensuring the availability of necessary materials.","core":true,"importance":3.21,"relevance":79.17,"frequency":2.58},{"id":18646,"text":"Deliver artwork on courier trips.","core":true,"importance":3.2,"relevance":83.33,"frequency":1.45},{"id":3811,"text":"Supervise and work with volunteers.","core":true,"importance":3,"relevance":87.5,"frequency":3.29},{"id":3828,"text":"Construct skeletal mounts of fossils, replicas of archaeological artifacts, or duplicate specimens, using a variety of materials and hand tools.","core":false,"importance":3,"relevance":45.83,"frequency":2.09},{"id":18645,"text":"Lead tours and teach educational courses to students and the general public.","core":false,"importance":2.96,"relevance":100,"frequency":2.21}],"activities":[{"id":"4.A.3.b.6","importance":4.77},{"id":"4.A.2.b.1","importance":4.73},{"id":"4.A.3.a.2","importance":4.73},{"id":"4.A.1.b.1","importance":4.54},{"id":"4.A.2.b.3","importance":4.52},{"id":"4.A.1.a.1","importance":4.5},{"id":"4.A.1.a.2","importance":4.35},{"id":"4.A.2.b.2","importance":4.35},{"id":"4.A.4.a.2","importance":4.31},{"id":"4.A.2.b.6","importance":4.08},{"id":"4.A.1.b.2","importance":3.96},{"id":"4.A.2.a.1","importance":3.92},{"id":"4.A.2.a.4","importance":3.92},{"id":"4.A.3.b.1","importance":3.88},{"id":"4.A.2.a.2","importance":3.81},{"id":"4.A.4.a.4","importance":3.77},{"id":"4.A.4.b.6","importa